INTENTIONAL DEVIATION FROM UPSTREAM: architect decision D4 (PR #4).

Formerly the oracle case testdata/upstream/unreadable; the inputs are unchanged.
The head-content fetch failed (head_status fetch_failed, no head.txt) and the
patch is empty, so every view renders the unreadable-file notice (upstream's
trigger, also review-mcp's under D3).

The notice is adapted from upstream's _unreadable_file_notice: the product
name "PR-Agent" is replaced by "review-mcp", so the model and the users see
the name of the tool they are actually running. The rest of the wording is
upstream's. internal/patch/literals.go holds the literal; NOTICE covers it
as adapted material.

How the outputs were derived: the upstream oracle (gen_goldens.py) was run
on a twin case with exactly these inputs, minus the "deviation" field. The
twin's outputs are byte-identical to the former oracle golden. Exactly one
substitution was then applied to every out.* file:

    "** PR-Agent failed"  ->  "** review-mcp failed"

See testdata/upstream/README.md, section "Deviations".
